re  which is for dongle pretty good at -150  desktop products go down to minus 160.  it does have this uh train of pulses in  here whenever these pulses are  symmetrical  uh on both sides of our 12 kilos tone we  know that they're jitter  there's other ones like i don't know if  these are symmetrical or not but there  are random ones you get that are not  symmetrical those are just spurious  noise that's just getting injected this  test doesn't just measure jitter  it measures anything that comes out of  the dac but in this  case we actually have a clear case of  jitter it it seems to be at  one kilohertz intervals that's that's  the  frame size of usb so that may be what's  causing it but the nice thing is that  the level's at -130 db  so definitely not audible and uh  you know well below audibility so it's  nice for dongle again for this class is  quite nice  so uh the most important thing in these  things is power  number one problem with these when they  they get distorted is because they just  don't have enough output tiny little  device can't have you know huge power  electronics in them and uh so it's very  important to measure power so as before  i've shown you with headphone amps we  start with a high impedance load  load like 300 ohm and here we only get  13 milliwatts  um my threshold here is 100 milliwatt  but for desktop products i'll show you  in a second how it ranks  but uh we go down here plug that into  every dongle of this type some of these  dongles are actually quite large so  these ones way up here are not tiny but  uh going all the way from uh little  dongles uh  like this i'm selling my my phone here  is actually here 3.4 milliwatt  power samsung phone that i have going  all the way up to this  helm one is 13.3 and you can see most of  the ones that  are in a good category are 13 to 14  there isn't anything that's this small  that puts out more power some of these  other ones have more power actually have  batteries in them and what have you 